{"event": "tool_call", "t": 1795231029.536, "name": "report", "arguments": {"verdict": "fixed", "root_cause": {"category": "logic", "model": "rpt_category_performance", "summary": "The model started from products and left-joined variants and order lines, so every product with no sales produced a row with a NULL sales_month, inflating unique_products per category with products that never sold. The report is a sales report, so the spine should be order lines, with variants and products joined as inner joins. Revenue, units and gross profit were already reconciled to the source and still do."}, "evidence": [{"kind": "query", "ref": "rpt_category_performance (before fix), order by sales_month nulls first", "finding": "Four NULL-month rows with 0 orders and NULL revenue, one per category (PHYSICAL 132 products, DIGITAL 8, SERVICE 6, GIFT_CARD 2). These are products with no order lines, counted in unique_products."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "stg_orders__order_lines vs rpt_category_performance", "finding": "Sum of line_total (722313.24) and quantity_ordered (6590) match the rpt totals exactly, both before and after the change, so no sales rows are lost."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "stg_orders__order_lines joined to stg_orders__orders", "finding": "18 order lines (164 joined rows, revenue 2950.78, PHYSICAL) point to ORPHAN-ORD-* order_ids missing from stg_orders__orders. They stay in the report as a NULL-month row, so revenue still reconciles, but this is a source data issue."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "stg_product__product_variants and stg_orders__order_lines grain", "finding": "variant_id is unique (1266 rows) and order_line_id is unique (3576 rows), so the join does not fan out sales."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "after fix rpt_category_performance", "finding": "Revenue 722313.24, units 6590, 199 rows. The NULL-month rows fall from 4 to 1 (only the orphan-order revenue remains)."}], "changes": [{"path": "models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql", "summary": "Ch