{"event": "report", "t": 1795231194.523, "claim": "fixed", "verdict": {"verdict": "fixed", "root_cause": {"category": "logic", "model": "rpt_category_performance", "summary": "The model started from products and left-joined variants and order lines, so every product with no sales produced a row with a NULL sales_month, inflating unique_products per category with products that never sold. The report is a sales report, so the spine should be order lines, with variants and products joined as inner joins. Revenue, units and gross profit were already reconciled to the source and still do."}, "evidence": [{"kind": "query", "ref": "rpt_category_performance (before fix), order by sales_month nulls first", "finding": "Four NULL-month rows with 0 orders and NULL revenue, one per category (PHYSICAL 132 products, DIGITAL 8, SERVICE 6, GIFT_CARD 2). These are products with no order lines, counted in unique_products."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "stg_orders__order_lines vs rpt_category_performance", "finding": "Sum of line_total (722313.24) and quantity_ordered (6590) match the rpt totals exactly, both before and after the change, so no sales rows are lost."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "stg_orders__order_lines joined to stg_orders__orders", "finding": "18 order lines (164 joined rows, revenue 2950.78, PHYSICAL) point to ORPHAN-ORD-* order_ids missing from stg_orders__orders. They stay in the report as a NULL-month row, so revenue still reconciles, but this is a source data issue."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "stg_product__product_variants and stg_orders__order_lines grain", "finding": "variant_id is unique (1266 rows) and order_line_id is unique (3576 rows), so the join does not fan out sales."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "after fix rpt_category_performance", "finding": "Revenue 722313.24, units 6590, 199 rows. The NULL-month rows fall from 4 to 1 (only the orphan-order revenue remains)."}], "changes": [{"path": "models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql", "summary": "Changed the FROM spine from products to order_lines, with inner joins to product_variants and products and a left join to orders. Products with no sales no longer produce NULL-month rows that inflate unique_products. Output columns, grain and materialization are unchanged, and totals still reconcile to the source."}], "confidence": "medium"}, "diffs": [{"path": "models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql", "diff": "--- a/models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql\n+++ b/models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql\n@@ -26,8 +26,8 @@\n     sum(ol.line_total) as revenue,\n     avg(ol.unit_price) as avg_unit_price,\n     sum(ol.line_total) - sum(ol.quantity_ordered * pv.cost_price) as gross_profit\n-from products p\n-left join product_variants pv on p.product_id = pv.product_id\n-left join order_lines ol on pv.variant_id = ol.variant_id\n+from order_lines ol\n+inner join product_variants pv on ol.variant_id = pv.variant_id\n+inner join products p on pv.product_id = p.product_id\n left join orders o on ol.order_id = o.order_id\n group by 1, 2\n"}], "text": "The verifier accepted the fix. The report is recorded, so I'm ending the run here.\n\n**Verdict: fixed (medium confidence).**\n\n**Root cause:** `rpt_category_performance` started from `products` and left-joined variants and order lines. Every product with no sales therefore produced a row with a NULL `sales_month`, and those rows inflated `unique_products` for each category. Before the fix there were four NULL-month rows: PHYSICAL (132 products), DIGITAL (8), SERVICE (6) and GIFT_CARD (2). None of them had orders or revenue.\n\n**Fix:** In `models/marts/product/rpt_category_performance.sql`, I changed the spine to `order_lines`, with inner joins to `product_variants` and `products` and a left join to `orders`. Output columns, grain and materialization are unchanged.\n\n**Evidence:**\n- Revenue (722,313.24) and units (6,590) match the source order lines exactly, before and after the change, so no sales rows are lost.\n- `variant_id` and `order_line_id` are unique in their staging tables, so the joins do not fan out.\n- After the fix the model builds and its tests pass. NULL-month rows fell from four to one.\n\n**Remaining issue (not fixed, source data):** 18 order lines reference `ORPHAN-ORD-*` order IDs that are missing from `stg_orders__orders`. Their revenue (2,950.78, PHYSICAL) is kept in a single NULL-month row. Revenue still reconciles, but those orders need fixing upstream.\n\n**Not addressed:** the build also showed a seed casing collision (`PRODUCT_CATEGORIES`) and many staging `not_null`/`unique` test failures. Those are outside this model and I did not touch them."}
